Subject: Product Info BLURT #1: Philmac 3G Product Confusion/Clarification

Hello All,

Keep in mind that 3G Philmac compression fittings are not just the IPS-OD v=
ersion.  3G is a modular product that serves 4 different product lines:  IP=
S-OD, IPS-ID, CTS, Kitec/QLine/XPA.

It is not enough to reference 3G Philmac.  You must identify which of the 4=
 types you are interested in.

For instance it is incorrect to ask for 3G and think that you have narrowed=
 your request to IPS-OD.  If a customer asks for 3G your response would be =
"what type, CTS, IPS-OD, IPS-ID, Kitec?"

Also is it possible in the same fitting to have "ends" that are different p=
roduct types.  For instance it would be possible to have a tee that had one=
 end IPS-OD, one end IPS-ID, and one end CTS.

The reference to Kitec/Qline/XPA is because the name of the pipe on which t=
his fitting is used has changed twice.  One customer may know it as Kitec, =
another as Qline, and yet another as XPA.

When in doubt, call me.

John

